{
  "sn2.26:0.1": "Linked Discourses 2.26 ",
  "sn2.26:0.2": "3. Various Sectarians ",
  "sn2.26:0.3": "With Rohitassa ",
  "sn2.26:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn2.26:1.2": "Standing to one side, the godling Rohitassa said to the Buddha: ",
  "sn2.26:1.3": "“Sir, is it possible to know or see or reach the end of the world by traveling to a place where there’s no being born, growing old, dying, passing away, or being reborn?” ",
  "sn2.26:1.4": "“Reverend, I say it’s not possible to know or see or reach the end of the world by traveling to a place where there’s no being born, growing old, dying, passing away, or being reborn.” ",
  "sn2.26:2.1": "“It’s incredible, sir, it’s amazing, ",
  "sn2.26:2.2": "how well said this was by the Buddha. ",
  "sn2.26:2.3": "",
  "sn2.26:3.1": "Once upon a time, I was a seer named Rohitassa, son of the benefactors. I was a sky-walker with psychic powers. ",
  "sn2.26:3.2": "I was as fast as a light arrow easily shot across the shadow of a palm tree by a well-trained expert archer with a strong bow. ",
  "sn2.26:3.3": "My stride was such that it could span from the eastern ocean to the western ocean. ",
  "sn2.26:3.4": "This wish came to me: ",
  "sn2.26:3.5": "‘I will reach the end of the world by traveling.’ ",
  "sn2.26:3.6": "Having such speed and stride, I traveled for my whole lifespan of a hundred years—pausing only to eat and drink, go to the toilet, and sleep to dispel weariness—and I passed away along the way, never reaching the end of the w